Secret Required Description <code>APP_CLIENT_ID</code> no Client ID of the org's automation App <code>APP_PRIVATE_KEY</code> no Private key of the org's automation App <p>The <code>report</code> job uses them to report the run to the org's operations queue (epic vergil-project/.github#1494), and the <code>refresh</code> job forwards them to <code>cd-docs.yml</code>, whose <code>docs</code> job deploys with an App token (see Behavior). They are declared optional, a release ahead of the reporting job, so every caller could pass them first. A run that does not pass them fails the deploy, with no fallback to <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code>, and a run from <code>develop</code> also turns <code>report</code> red. Pass them:</p> <pre><code>    secrets: inherit
</code></pre> <p>The App keys live only in the caller's <code>automation</code> environment (epic vergil-project/.github#1384), and <code>secrets: inherit</code> carries them to this workflow from a caller in the same organization. <code>inherit</code> reaches only a reusable workflow in the caller's own organization or enterprise, so a caller in another organization passes the keys by name instead, as logical-minds-foundry/docs#44 does:</p> <pre><code>    secrets:
      APP_CLIENT_ID: ${{ secrets.APP_CLIENT_ID }}
      APP_PRIVATE_KEY: ${{ secrets.APP_PRIVATE_KEY }}
</code></pre>
